.TH tkudavbrowser n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkudavbrowser
.PP
A read\-only navigation pane for a CalDAV/CardDAV server, built on \fBtclutils::tudav\fR. It lists the server's collections grouped by kind (Calendars / Address Books / Other) in a \fBttk::treeview\fR; selecting a collection fires \fB\-oncollection\fR so an app can load its contents into \fBtkuvcard\fR / \fBtkutodo\fR.
.CS
set b [tkudavbrowser::widget .b -oncollection {apply {{w info} {
    # info = {href .. displayname .. kind ..}
    puts "open [dict get $info kind]: [dict get $info href]"
}}}]
pack $b -fill both -expand 1

tkudavbrowser::setClient .b $davClient   ;# a tclutils::tudav client
tkudavbrowser::refresh .b                ;# discover + listCollections (network)

tkudavbrowser::collections .b            ;# flat list of {href displayname kind}
tkudavbrowser::selected .b               ;# current selection dict, or {}
.CE
.PP
\fBrefresh\fR runs \fBtudav::discover\fR then \fBlistCollections\fR on both home sets, de\-duplicating by href (Radicale, for instance, uses one home set for both kinds). It is \fBsynchronous\fR and may block briefly. For offline rendering or testing, \fBsetData $path $collections\fR accepts a ready list of \fB{href displayname kind}\fR dicts and builds the tree without any network I/O.
.SS "Provisioning (opt\-in)"
.PP
With \fB\-editable 1\fR the widget adds a small bar to create and delete collections:
.CS
tkudavbrowser::createCalendar    .b "Sprint Board"   ;# -> new path, then refresh
tkudavbrowser::createAddressbook .b "Team"
tkudavbrowser::deleteCollection  .b ?href?           ;# selected if href omitted
.CE
.PP
New collections are created under the discovered home set (path = home + slug\-of\-name + \fB/\fR) via \fBtudav::mkCalendar\fR / \fBmkAddressbook\fR; \fBdeleteCollection\fR uses \fBtudav::delete\fR. All three refresh the tree afterwards and are network operations (call \fBrefresh\fR once first so the home set is known, else \fB{TKUTILS TKDAVBROWSER NOHOME}\fR).
.PP
Pairs with \fBtkudavaccount\fR (connect) on one side and \fBtkuvcard\fR / \fBtkutodo\fR (content) on the other.
.SS "Additional exported commands"
.PP
Documented for completeness (same module, also covered by the test suite):
.CS
tkudavbrowser::treeWidget path                 ;# return the internal ttk::treeview widget path (for custom bindings or styling)
.CE
